From: Eris Linux maintainers
Subject: [PATCH] gdb: handle readlink errors from the mount namespace helper

A failed readlink is returned by the helper as result -1 and an empty
payload. Handle this before comparing the payload length with the result,
otherwise remote library access can abort gdbserver for container targets.
Preserve errno when receiving the helper message itself fails.

Upstream-Status: Pending

--- a/gdb/nat/linux-namespaces.c
+++ b/gdb/nat/linux-namespaces.c
@@ -1040,12 +1040,15 @@
   size = mnsh_recv_intstr (helper, &ret, &error, buf, bufsiz);
 
   if (size < 0)
-    {
-      ret = -1;
+    return -1;
+
+  if (ret < 0)
+    {
       errno = error;
-    }
-  else
-    gdb_assert (size == ret);
+      return -1;
+    }
+
+  gdb_assert (size == ret);
 
   return ret;
 }
